<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Gmquest</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>gmquest &lt;player&gt; easy|fair|hard &lt;quest name&gt;[: what they did]     (230)
gmquest &lt;player&gt;
</pre>
<p>Makes a game master's event one of the player's quests, once they've 
played it through to its end. "&lt;quest name&gt; Complete" goes into the 
list <a cmd='#'>Help Quests</a> shows them, with what they did, and they earn 
experience by their level and how hard it was: a tenth (<b>easy</b>), a 
quarter (<b>fair</b>) or half (<b>hard</b>) of the experience between 
their level and the next. The player sees "You have completed a quest" 
and what they earned, and you see how much it was.
</p><p>Each quest name counts once per player, and is at most 50 letters. 
Gods get neither quests nor experience this way.
</p><p><b>gmquest &lt;player&gt;</b> alone lists the game-master quests they have 
done, and their level.
</p><p>Example:
</p>
<pre>gmquest asta fair The Lost Flint Box: found the old dwarf's flint box
</pre>
<p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Quests</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Gmtreasure</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Experience</a>
</pre>




</div>